{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/859749-the-nature-of-the-beast","id":859749,"title":"The nature of the beast","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-05T10:52:05-07:00","id":859749,"title":"The nature of the beast","content":"In the topic on the different type of strix I've wrote that i try to develop different personnalities based on a characters clan. While a gangrel frenzying would fall on all four and start to growl, a mekhet frenzying would disappear and close all the lights and lock all the door. I know that doesnt strictly follow the rules of frenzy. Lately i've been thinking on ways to make the vampire's beast something both more present and more subtle in a vampire's unlife. <br /> Now frenzy are fine to represent the beast taking control in instinctual respond. But i also want something that engage the character more often.<br /> <br /> So far the only idea i've had is to have each player choose a 'dark aspiration'. Following that aspiration would always be a breaking point and (as normal for aspiration) would give a beat.<br /> I like the idea that it both tempts the character and the player into endangering his humanity for power. Also i wouldnt put following the aspiration on a roll (willpower or otherwise) as i want it to be less an overt control of the character. <br /> <br /> Do you have other methods or tools that you have used to make the beast something more present in the vampires unlives???","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-ma